# Kernel-config delta: what our features need that the base target does NOT
# already carry.
#
# Read the two files this is measured against before changing anything here:
#   OVL rtl8197f config : /tmp/rebase/openwrt-rx23302/openwrt/target/linux/
#                         rtl819x/rtl8197f/config-6.18          (251 lines)
#   OVL target config   : .../rtl819x/config-6.18               (1 line: NVMEM)
#   BASE generic config : openwrt@82e2e4f4 target/linux/generic/config-6.18
# Line numbers below are from those files as pinned (BASE_REV 82e2e4f4,
# OVERLAY_REV 80e62b6).
#
# WHERE THESE LINES BELONG
#   Append the "ADD" block to OVL rtl8197f/config-6.18 (i.e. ship it as our
#   whole-file replacement in files/target/linux/rtl819x/rtl8197f/config-6.18,
#   and expect build.sh to report it as a clobbered overlay file).
#   Anything that must WIN over that file goes in the seed as
#   CONFIG_KERNEL_<SYM> instead: .config-level CONFIG_KERNEL_* knobs are
#   injected after the target config merge and silently override it. That is
#   where the 4.14 line kept crashlog off, and it is why the two CRASHLOG/PSTORE
#   notes below are phrased as "no action" rather than as seed lines.
#
# ===========================================================================
# ADD - symbols our own work needs, absent from OVL rtl8197f/config-6.18
# ===========================================================================
#
# --- 1. rootfs split for a cr6c container (track 02 decides whether this is
#         needed at all) ---------------------------------------------------
# OVL ships NO cvimg parser: `grep -i cvimg` over their config-6.18 finds
# nothing, and BASE's mtdsplit directory has no mtdsplit_cvimg.c either
# (target/linux/generic/files/drivers/mtd/mtdsplit/ at 82e2e4f4 lists
# bcm63xx..wrgg, no cvimg). Their board uses fixed-partitions instead.
# Our KernelFS is one container whose squashfs offset is 16+len, UNALIGNED
# (FACTS §4, README: 0x3c0812), so a fixed-partitions rootfs window only works
# if the image recipe pins the kernel size; with mtdsplit the geometry is
# discovered. Both are legitimate; if track 02 keeps the parser from our
# files/target/linux/generic/files/drivers/mtd/mtdsplit/, these two lines are
# what make it exist:
CONFIG_MTD_SPLIT_CVIMG_FW=y
# CONFIG_MTD_SPLIT_FIRMWARE_NAME is already "firmware" in BASE
# (target/linux/generic/config-6.18:4120) - do NOT restate it, and note that
# the parser only runs on a partition named exactly that (README risk #3).
#
# ★ HOW the parser gets into the kernel tree, because our 4.14 way is now a
#   cross-target regression. BASE delivers the mtdsplit directory from
#   target/linux/generic/files/drivers/mtd/mtdsplit/{Kconfig,Makefile}, and our
#   files/ overlay replaces BOTH of those whole files with the 4.14-era
#   versions: ours declares 16 config symbols, BASE declares 22, and the seven
#   we would delete are MTD_SPLIT_{BCM63XX,CFE_BOOTFS,ELF,H3C_VFS,SEIL,
#   MSTC_BOOT,OPENWRT_PROLOG}_FW (measured by diffing the two files at
#   BASE_REV). mtdsplit is a GENERIC directory: dropping those breaks other
#   targets' configs, not ours.
#   The cheap fix is additive: keep only mtdsplit_cvimg.c in files/ (a new file,
#   no conflict), delete our Kconfig/Makefile copies, and append the two
#   stanzas with a patch. That works because the files/ copy happens BEFORE the
#   patch dirs are applied - include/quilt.mk:92 defines
#   kernel_files=$(foreach fdir,$(GENERIC_FILES_DIR) $(FILES_DIR),$(fdir)/.) and
#   quilt.mk:96 copies it, while the generic backport/pending/hack and the
#   target's own patches-6.18 are applied at quilt.mk:102-105.
#
# Already carried by OVL, do not duplicate: CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y (:113),
# CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR_USE_4K_SECTORS=y (:114 - the symbol still exists in 6.18,
# BASE generic:4111), CONFIG_MTD_ROOTFS_ROOT_DEV=y (:115, and BASE generic:4101),
# CONFIG_MTD_SPLIT_FIRMWARE=y (:116), and CONFIG_MTD_SPLIT_SQUASHFS_ROOT is
# deliberately off (:117) because that splitter puts rootfs_data right after the
# squashfs body - exactly where the Tenda loader keeps its checksum. Keep it off
# and say so: the same trap the rx23302 comment describes is ours verbatim.
#
# Our 4.14 subtarget config had CONFIG_MTD_M25P80=y. That symbol no longer
# exists: BASE generic/config-6.18 has no MTD_M25P80 line at all (the SPI-NOR
# chip layer was folded into MTD_SPI_NOR), so restating it would just be
# dropped by the config sanitizer.
#
# --- 2. squashfs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to add. BASE generic:6877 CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y and :6892
# CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y, and the mangled-magic trick is a stock-kernel patch we
# must NOT copy (FACTS §4, README risk #4): our kernel matches plain hsqs and
# mtdsplit.c matches SQUASHFS_MAGIC.
#
# --- 3. switch + ethernet (FACTS §5) ---------------------------------------
# Nothing to add for the RTL8367RB path: OVL already builds it IN, not as
# modules - CONFIG_SWCONFIG=y (:208), CONFIG_SWCONFIG_LEDS=y (:209),
# CONFIG_RTL8366_SMI=y (:230), CONFIG_RTL8367B_PHY=y (:231),
# CONFIG_PHYLINK=y (:229), CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY=y (:227), CONFIG_PHYLIB=y (:179),
# CONFIG_MDIO_BUS=y (:99), CONFIG_FWNODE_MDIO=y (:49), and the SoC ethernet
# engine CONFIG_NET_RTL819X=y (:225).
# ★ Because NET_RTL819X=y is built-in, there is NO kmod to select in the seed,
#   and a built-in driver cannot link against a modular nf_flow_table. OVL
#   measures 857-929 Mbit/s with exactly this arrangement plus
#   kmod-nft-offload, so the first CI build is the check: if kconf warns or the
#   link fails on net/flow_offload symbols, make CONFIG_NET_RTL819X=m and add
#   the matching kmod package instead of patching around it.
#
# --- 4. LEDs (track 03 - only when the DTS declares them) ------------------
# OVL has LED_TRIGGER_PHY=y (:96) but no LED driver at all. BASE leaves
# CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO off (generic:3322). Our 4.14 subtarget config had it =y
# after finding that an LED node without a provider binds nothing; the Tenda
# pins are still unverified, and a wrong GPIO line held the switch in reset on
# the reference board (README risk #9). Add it TOGETHER WITH the DTS nodes, not
# before:
#CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO=y            <- uncomment with track 03's led nodes
#
# --- 5. ramoops / pstore: leave OFF, on purpose ----------------------------
# Nothing to add, and nothing to remove: BASE generic already has
# # CONFIG_PSTORE is not set (generic:5155) and # CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM is not set
# (:5162), and OVL does not enable it. That is the state the DIR-842 TX wedge
# required (4.14 config-4.14: "pstore is OFF ENTIRELY... an attached ramoops
# WEDGES CPU-originated frames"), so it is inherited, not re-litigated. If a
# future experiment wants pstore anyway, it needs CONFIG_PSTORE=y +
# CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y + CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y AND a /reserved-memory node in
# the DTS - config alone would be the silent half-fix.
#
# --- 6. symbolised oops on a board that has never booted --------------------
# BASE generic ships # CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set (generic:3181) and OVL keeps
# DEBUG_INFO=y (:37) without it, i.e. a first oops prints addresses only. On
# this platform the whole debugging method so far has been reading traces off
# a serial line, and the 4.14 line's crashlog work was about SEEING the first
# oops. Costs a few hundred KB of kernel; the container budget is 15.5 MiB of
# KernelFS and the loader's own limit is the decompressed kernel (< 16 MiB,
# FACTS §3), so this is affordable - but it is a size decision, so it is listed
# rather than asserted:
CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y
#CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y         <- only if module symbols are actually needed
#
# --- 7. crashlog: no action, the feature is gone ---------------------------
# The 4.14 seed's "# CONFIG_KERNEL_CRASHLOG is not set" cannot be ported
# because there is nothing to switch off: BASE generic/config-6.18 has no
# CONFIG_CRASHLOG line and target/linux/generic/hack-6.18/ carries no crashlog
# patch (the 6xx range there is 650-netfilter-add-xt_FLOWOFFLOAD-target.patch).
# Do not re-add the seed line: a symbol that no longer exists is the one seed
# bug that shows up as nothing at all.
#
# --- 8. PCI, when 5 GHz is attempted (track 06 only) -----------------------
# OVL ships the PCIe host code (files-6.18/arch/mips/pci/pci-realtek.c +
# patches-6.18/0005-pci-realtek.patch, 0006-realtek-have-pci.patch) but leaves
# PCI off: # CONFIG_PCI is not set (rtl8197f/config-6.18:244), with PCI_HCI=y
# at :243 for the embedded 2.4 GHz radio. RTL8832BR is on PCIe, so track 06
# will have to set at least:
#CONFIG_PCI=y
#CONFIG_PCI_REALTEK_HAS_PCI=y   <- name comes from 0006-realtek-have-pci.patch;
#                                  re-read that patch before using this line
#
# ===========================================================================
# GONE / RENAMED - 4.14 symbols with no 6.18 equivalent (do not port them)
# ===========================================================================
# CONFIG_MTD_M25P80=y        -> folded into CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR (no such line in
#                               BASE generic/config-6.18)
# CONFIG_RTL8192CD=m         -> replaced by the in-tree HAL: OVL :238-246
#                               CONFIG_WLAN_HAL=y, WLAN_HAL_88XX=y,
#                               WLAN_HAL_8197F=y, RTL8192FE_RX23302=y and the
#                               WEXT block :247-250. Note their config-6.18:233
#                               -237 comment: built IN, a driver that hangs in
#                               rtl8192cd_init_one takes the boot with it.
#                               Track 05 owns the choice of =y vs =m and the
#                               board-specific RTL8192FE_* symbol name.
# CONFIG_RTL8197F_WMAC=y     -> no such symbol here (0 hits in BASE tree); the
#                               HAL above is the WMAC path now.
# CONFIG_CRASHLOG /          -> gone, see §7.
# CONFIG_KERNEL_CRASHLOG
# CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_IPV4/6,-> removed in 6.x netfilter; OVL uses the unified
# CONFIG_NF_NAT_IPV4 etc.      NF_CONNTRACK=y style lines (:152-161)
# CONFIG_MIPS_CMDLINE_FROM_DTB=y stays (:106) - our DTS carries the chosen
#                               bootargs, so the cmdline still comes from the
#                               DTB, and CONFIG_CMDLINE from the loader is the
#                               other half (LOADER_DATA in image/Makefile:34).
